            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for a loophole, then the Gujarati for a proposal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: સમાધાન",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સમાધાન — samādhān — \"a compromise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "જો તમે બંને બેસીને વાત કરશો તો સમાધાન થશે. jo tame banne besīne vāt karśo to samādhān thaśe. If you two sit down and talk, you'll reach a compromise."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સમાધાન (samādhān) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit samādhāna, \"putting together\" (Monier-Williams); in Gujarati it is the settling of a quarrel."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
